            "label": "initial geometry and dynamics characterization",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.initial_physics"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial decision is whether the first intervention should target geometric branch/limit selection or closed-loop settling authority. A dense official-range grid tests whether any target is infeasible or angle/radius localized, while compiled dynamics and multi-configuration torque probes quantify the authority available to arrest motion at the 50 Hz control interval. This evidence is more decision-relevant than an unstratified initial training result."
